# ---- Numbers -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Spoken number words. 21-99 are said the inverted way, one word: "dvaadvacet", "pětatřicet",
# "jedenadvacet" (21, 31 ... 91 are listed): with a noun Czech then takes the genitive plural for
# every number from 5 up ("dvaadvacet tahů", "jedenadvacet chyb"), which is the plural rule of
# assets/i18n (one: 1 | few: 2-4 | other: 0, 5+), where "dvacet dva" would need "dvacet dva tahy".
# 101-999 compose as "{hundreds} {rest}" ("sto dvaadvacet"); every hundred is listed.
# Forms (a number without its own form falls back to the plain word):
#   m     masculine "jeden" ("jeden tah", "jeden pěšec")
#   f     feminine "jedna", "dvě" ("jedna chyba", "dvě chyby")
#   neut  neuter "jedno", "dvě" ("jedno pole", "dvě pole")
#   ma    masculine animate accusative "jednoho" ("vzít jednoho pěšce")
#   fa    feminine accusative "jednu", "dvě" ("udělat jednu chybu")
